## ⏱ Time and Space Complexity

| Metric            | Complexity |
|-------------------|------------|
| Time Complexity   | `O(n)` — each node visited once |
| Space Complexity  | `O(h)` — recursion stack, where `h` is tree height |

---

## 🎯 Final Thoughts
This solution is efficient because it combines **height calculation** and **balance checking** in a single recursive pass. By returning `-1` when imbalance is detected, it avoids redundant computations and ensures early termination. It’s a classic example of a bottom-up recursive strategy that optimizes performance in tree problems.


